# Synapse Context Compiler — .clinerules (v2)
# Replace v1 .clinerules entirely.

## Tech stack
# v1 (do not modify):
- Go 1.25.5+  (mcp-go v1.1.0 raises the floor; go.mod declares it)
- sqlite-vec v0.1.x  (github.com/asg017/sqlite-vec-go-bindings)
- onnxruntime-go v1.31.0 (github.com/yalue/onnxruntime_go)
  model pinned: ca2c6b84644f6c2f4b7c879851ad9d364ae375f6
- tiktoken-go         (github.com/pkoukk/tiktoken-go)
- chi v5              (github.com/go-chi/chi/v5)
- go-yaml v3          (gopkg.in/yaml.v3)
- testify v1          (github.com/stretchr/testify)
- charmbracelet/log   (structured logging)
- google/uuid

# v2 additions:
- pgx v5              (github.com/jackc/pgx/v5)
- pgvector-go         (github.com/pgvector/pgvector-go)
- golang-jwt/jwt v5   (github.com/golang-jwt/jwt/v5)
- mcp-go              (github.com/mark3labs/mcp-go)
- crypto/hmac         (stdlib — no new dependency)

## v1 internals — do NOT modify unless a v2 bug explicitly requires it:
  proxy, classifier, scorer, store, embedder, dedup, budget,
  compiler, api, config, retrieval, supersession, trace

## v2 internals:
  plane, sync, conflict, ledger, mcp, tenant, metering, billing

## Coding style (unchanged from v1)
- goroutines + channels, not callbacks
- interfaces for every external dependency
- no global state — constructor injection
- max 300 lines per file
- camelCase unexported, PascalCase exported, kebab-case config keys
- fmt.Errorf("module: %w", err) for all error wrapping
- charmbracelet/log for structured logging
- comments on all exported types and functions
- verify with real go test output before treating any fix as confirmed

## v2 hard rules
- NEVER UPDATE or DELETE rows in the ledger table — append-only
- NEVER use row-level filter as sole tenant isolation — schema-per-tenant required
- NEVER log JWT secrets, HMAC signing keys, or tenant API keys
- MCP tools MUST share the same sanitization pipeline as REST
- Conflict resolution MUST keep both memory versions with conflict marker
- Control plane MUST boot with zero external deps other than Postgres
- ListenAddr for plane defaults to 127.0.0.1:9090 — never 0.0.0.0
- SYNAPSE_JWT_SECRET and SYNAPSE_DB_DSN from env only — fatal if missing in prod
- MCP responses MUST include score breakdown (S/R/I/T) and trace_id
  so users can see WHY a memory was surfaced (differentiation from OpenMemory MCP)

## v1 rules (still apply — no exceptions)
- Default bind 127.0.0.1:8080 — never 0.0.0.0
- Authorization AND x-api-key headers NEVER in any log output
- All Synapse-created files: 0600 permissions
- Memory content sanitized before storage
- Traces in-memory only unless --persist-traces

## Phase discipline
- One Cline session per phase (build)
- One separate Cline session per phase (debug) — never debug in the build chat
- Do not implement Phase N+1 features while in Phase N
- Update PROGRESS.md after each phase before closing
- Do not install new dependencies without explicit confirmation
- Verify every fix with real go test output from your terminal